ight again. That child would be Jesus."],"layers":[{"id":"gate","kind":"plate","depth":0.1,"paint":"gate","src":"art/garden/promise/gate.jpg"}],"effects":[{"type":"motes","from":0},{"type":"rays","from":1,"x":0.72,"y":0.2,"soft":true},{"type":"starmaker","from":1,"sky":0.25}],"touch":{"hint":"Tap the sky","at":[0.5,0.15]},"sound":{"ambience":["wind"],"mood":"dawn"},"frame":[0.66,0.5],"stickers":[{"id":"promise","name":"The Promise","earn":"play","at":[0.7,0.3],"r":0.12}],"lamb":{"at":[0.78,0.6],"size":0.03},"spots":[{"at":[0.725,0.15],"fx":"twinkle","sound":"twinkle","hit":0.05,"size":1.3},{"at":[0.47,0.25],"fx":"leaves","sound":"rustle","hit":0.06}]}],"next":{"story":"noah","title":"Noah's Ark","sub":"Genesis 6:9 – 9:17: the story of a flood, a boat and a promise."},"talk":{"questions":["Why do you think Adam and Eve hid from God?","Have you ever done something wrong and wanted to hide? What helps you say sorry?","God still loved Adam and Eve, and made them a promise. How does God show us He loves us?"],"verse":{"ref":"Genesis 3:9","text":"But the LORD God called out to the man, “Where are you?”"}}}